Layer-0 MLP feature that is strongest on words that open or name a Python method or
class: `def`, `self` (and `(self`, `__init__(`), and a non-Java `class`. Weaker on
jump words (`goto`, `break`, `yield`, `next`). Slightly negative on primitive type
names (`bool`, `int`, `Integer`, `boolean`), which appear in typed languages.
Java/C#-style `public class` is treated as no signal. Everything else is 0.
Most of the component's variance is diffuse token-level noise that a short program
does not capture; this program captures only the concept peaks.
