"""A comma/list-separator detector with grammatical context.

Bare commas are negative, especially near the beginning of a document,
after numbers, discourse markers, or mixed-case identifiers.
More words in the recent clause/line and a subordinator near the clause
start soften the response.
Surplus opening brackets strengthen it. Context is capped at 400 characters
and resets at document boundaries.
Commas fused with other punctuation have smaller responses; a following
blank line nearly cancels them. End-of-text markers are positive.
