"""Word-internal en syllables and a few smaller spelling responses.

The main response is to short en/end/ens syllables. A preceding consonant,
a vowel in the ASCII word tail, and recent German function words strengthen
it. Completing open-/eigen- spellings across a token boundary is strong;
a lone capital initial is weaker. Other short e-syllables, consonant
clusters, y-clusters, and German endings get smaller responses. Two
separate rules handle a partial Japanese long-vowel token and a tool tag.
These are spelling heuristics, not a full language or word parser.
