A decimal/version dot after an ASCII digit gives the strongest usual pulse.
Dots after words or merged with punctuation give smaller pulses; ellipses and
patent .sub./.sup. notation give only a small one. A document-initial dot gives
an extra-strong pulse. Non-digits predict zero: a dot arms a new pulse,
while other tokens clear it. State is reset at each document boundary.
