"""layers.0.mlp.down_proj:3700 - a "dotted name" detector.

The component fires on a token that starts with a dot and continues a name with
no space: the dot-segments of hostnames ("cloud.mail.ru", "www.x.com"), Java/Go
package paths ("org.springframework.data", "java.util.List") and file names
("README.md"). The same dot after an object in code ("self.image", "console.log",
"holder.itemView") or a file extension ("main.py", "app.js") gives nothing.

The program predicts that strength, in plain terms:
  - a dot-word token (".com", ".gr", ".world") starts at a base of 0.7;
  - a single letter after the dot (".x", ".v", ".b") is stronger (+0.4);
  - inside a URL or an import/package line it is stronger (+0.4);
  - file extensions (.py, .js, .ts, .html, ...) are weaker (-0.5), common code
    method names (.append, .push, .println, ...) weaker (-0.25), and a capitalised
    name (.URL, .Test, .IOException) weaker (-0.4);
  - in code (self, this, console, function, def) it is weaker (-0.2).
Everything else is 0. Values are clipped at 0.
"""

