"""Detect inline dash punctuation, with a weaker response to familiar separators.

En dashes generally give the strongest negative response. Word/number
joiners differ from newline-initial list markers. Most responses weaken
when the same separator spelling repeats; spaced em-dash predictions
approach zero in repetitive separator sequences. The very first token
gets fixed startup values. Small word-specific activations are not modeled.
