"""A negative response to acute e, especially short spelling pieces.
Four French participle/agreement endings (é, és, ée, ées) receive explicit
strengths. Other acute-e pieces weaken with surrounding letters. Capitals
strengthen the response; a short or capitalized preceding stem strengthens
an unspaced ending. Other accents and encoded punctuation respond weakly.
